(7507723, 1197516, 185714, '<td valign="top">I had seen image from the same environment, not sure you are the same person.<br/> <br/>Here are my point of view to your image:<br/> <br/>1.	Focus<br/>Currently your focus is out.  There are few factors affecting your focus  shutter speed is not enough or either the model had moved.   You need to shoot wide open say F/4 and pump up your ISO if necessary.  Aim at the eyes when you shoot (IMO - in my own opinion)<br/> <br/>2.	Composition<br/>Do watch out for the background.  Avoid overlapping.  Right now your model has overlapped with the guy behind. Tried moving to the left.<br/> <br/>I feel, in this instance, Point 1 (focus) is crucial, at least to get the viewer attention.  <br/> <br/>Hope this helps.</td>', 'I had seen image from the same environment, not sure you are the same person. Here are my point of view to your image: 1.	FocusCurrently your focus is out.  There are few factors affecting your focus  shutter speed is not enough or either the model had moved.   You need to shoot wide open say F/4 and pump up your ISO if necessary.  Aim at the eyes when you shoot (IMO - in my own opinion) 2.	CompositionDo watch out for the background.  Avoid overlapping.  Right now your model has overlapped with the guy behind. Tried moving to the left. I feel, in this instance, Point 1 (focus) is crucial, at least to get the viewer attention.   Hope this helps.', '2017-04-04 23:09:01.000000', NULL, 1),
